格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"deepseek harness plugin obsidian memory","id":"gh:1335820386","install_available":true,"language":"JavaScript","name":"dsh-client-ui-obsidian-memory","slug":"detongz/dsh-client-ui-obsidian-memory","topics":["dsh-plugin","dsh-plugins"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"deepseek harness plugin obsidian memory"},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# dsh-client-ui-obsidian-memory"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"> 🧠 Obsidian Memory for DeepSeek Harness — persistent memory via local Markdown vault"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"A DSH plugin that gives your AI agent **persistent memory** backed by a local Obsidian (or plain Mar"},{"id":"p4s2","text":"kdown) vault. It registers 5 file-system tools (`obsidian_memory_*`) and renders a sidebar panel sho"},{"id":"p4s3","text":"wing vault status and tool reference."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"Inspired by @Saccc_c's Codex memory techniques."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"## What it does"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"- **5 memory tools** — AI can read, list, search, write, and append to your local vault\n- **Sidebar "},{"id":"p7s2","text":"panel** — a vault directory browser, opened from a sidebar panel icon; the panel mounts in the layou"},{"id":"p7s3","text":"t's `main` slot (see Known issues for version caveats)\n- **No external server** — talks directly to "},{"id":"p7s4","text":"the file system via DSH's host runtime\n- **Codex-compatible** — works with the `Codex/` directory st"},{"id":"p7s5","text":"ructure recommended by the community"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"### Available Tools"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"| Tool | Action |"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"| `obsidian_memory_read` | Read a Markdown or text file |\n| `obsidian_memory_list` | List files and "},{"id":"p10s2","text":"directories |\n| `obsidian_memory_search` | Full-text search across `.md` and `.txt` files |\n| `obsid"},{"id":"p10s3","text":"ian_memory_write` | Write or overwrite a file |\n| `obsidian_memory_append` | Append content to the e"},{"id":"p10s4","text":"te` | Write or overwrite a file |\n| `obsidian_memory_append` | Append content to the end of a file |"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"## Quick Start"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"### 1. Prepare your vault"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"Create a `Codex/` folder anywhere on your machine (e.g. inside an Obsidian vault):"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"### 2. Install the plugin"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"One command, from anywhere:"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"> The plugin ships a `dsh.bundle` manifest, so `dsh plugin add` both installs\n> the package **and** "},{"id":"p18s2","text":"activates it as a profile layer (the bundled\n> `cordis.patch.yml` inserts the `obsidian-memory` entr"},{"id":"p18s3","text":"y). No manual\n> `cordis.patch.yml` edit is needed to load the plugin."},{"id":"p19s1","text":"### 3. Configure your vault path"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"Point the plugin at your `Codex/` folder. In your profile's `cordis.patch.yml`:"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"Replace `vaultPath` with the **absolute path** to your `Codex/` folder.\nAlternatively set the enviro"},{"id":"p22s2","text":"nment variable `OBSIDIAN_VAULT_PATH`."},{"id":"p23s1","text":"### 4. Restart DSH"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"After restart:\n- The **5 tools** are available to the AI when `vaultPath` is configured\n- The sideba"},{"id":"p25s2","text":"r panel does **not** currently appear — see Known issues"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"## Requirements & compatibility"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"| Requirement | Verified |"},{"id":"p28s1","text":"| Node.js | **≥ 22** (verified on 22.22.2). DSH itself does not start on Node 18 (`node:util` has no"},{"id":"p28s2","text":" `parseEnv`) or Node 20 (silent exit), so no lower floor is claimed. |\n| DSH | `0.1.1-rc.2`, `0.1.2-"},{"id":"p28s3","text":"alpha.5`, `0.1.2-rc.1`, `0.1.5-alpha.1`, `0.1.5-alpha.2`, `0.1.5-rc.1`, `0.1.5-rc.2`, `0.1.6-alpha.1"},{"id":"p28s4","text":"` — all verified 9/9 |\n| DSH profile | `web` (only the web profile was exercised) |"},{"id":"p29s1","text":"The exact per-version verdict lives in `package.json` under\n`dsh.compatibility.dshReleases`. Every `"},{"id":"p29s2","text":"compatible` entry is backed by a real\ninstall → start → uninstall run in a throwaway `DSH_HOME`; `0."},{"id":"p29s3","text":"1.3-alpha.1` and\n`0.1.3-alpha.2` are declared `unknown` because they could not be tested (no\npublish"},{"id":"p29s4","text":"ed artifact; a failing CLI install). See\ndocs/COMPATIBILITY.md for the full matrix, the evidence\nmet"},{"id":"p29s5","text":"hod and the reproduction command."},{"id":"p30s1","text":"### Permissions and risk"},{"id":"p31s1","text":"The plugin runs with the DSH host process's privileges and touches the file\nsystem directly:"},{"id":"p32s1","text":"- **File access** — reads and writes inside the directory given by `vaultPath`.\nPaths are sandboxed:"},{"id":"p32s2","text":" `..` traversal outside the vault is refused.\n- **Network** — none. The plugin makes no outbound req"},{"id":"p32s3","text":"uests and bundles no\nserver.\n- **Commands / credentials** — none.\n- **Lifecycle scripts** — `prepare"},{"id":"p32s4","text":"` (runs `npm run build`). Declared explicitly;\nit only ever runs `rolldown` locally. The built `lib/"},{"id":"p32s5","text":"` is committed, so a\ngit-based install is self-contained."},{"id":"p33s1","text":"Read access to a vault means the AI can read anything inside `vaultPath`. Point\nit at a dedicated `C"},{"id":"p33s2","text":"odex/` folder rather than a whole personal vault."},{"id":"p34s1","text":"## Known issues"},{"id":"p35s1","text":"### The sidebar panel now renders (since 0.4.1)"},{"id":"p36s1","text":"The client half registers a global panel icon in the `sidebar.panellist` slot\n(`id: \"obsidian-memory"},{"id":"p36s2","text":"\"`, `order: 50`, label \"Obsidian Memory\") and the vault\nbrowser in the layout's `main` slot under th"},{"id":"p36s3","text":"e same key. Clicking the sidebar\nicon calls `ctx.layout.selectPanel(\"obsidian-memory\")`, which opens"},{"id":"p36s4","text":" the panel in\nthe central column. This works on DSH versions that declare the `sidebar.panellist`\nli"},{"id":"p36s5","text":"st slot and the keyed `main` slot (verified on the `0.1.5` / `0.1.6` line)."},{"id":"p37s1","text":"On DSH versions released before those slots existed, the two `ctx.slots.inject`\ncalls are simply ine"},{"id":"p37s2","text":"rt: the plugin still loads, the 5 `obsidian_memory_*` tools\nstill work, and the sidebar icon simply "},{"id":"p37s3","text":"does not appear. No crash, no install\nfailure — only the panel is unavailable on those older builds."},{"id":"p38s1","text":"**The five `obsidian_memory_*` tools are unaffected** on every version above."},{"id":"p39s1","text":"### Build reproducibility (fixed in 0.4.0)"},{"id":"p40s1","text":"Before 0.4.0 the committed `lib/` depended on the absolute path of the checkout:\nrolldown's `//#regi"},{"id":"p40s2","text":"on` comment embedded the CSS virtual module id, lightningcss\nmixed the `filename` into its `[hash]` "},{"id":"p40s3","text":"CSS-module prefix, and its export order\nwas not stable. `npm run build` now produces byte-identical "},{"id":"p40s4","text":"output from any\ndirectory, so the committed bundle matches a rebuild at the same Commit."},{"id":"p41s1","text":"## Architecture"},{"id":"p42s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p43s1","text":"| Component | Role |"},{"id":"p44s1","text":"| **Host** (`lib/index.js`) | Node side: registers tools, reads/writes vault files |\n| **Client** (`"},{"id":"p44s2","text":"lib/client.js`) | Browser side: sidebar panel with static tool reference |\n| **Vault** | Data source"},{"id":"p44s3","text":": local Markdown files |"},{"id":"p45s1","text":"### Compatibility harness"},{"id":"p46s1","text":"`scripts/verify-disposable-profile.mjs` runs the full install → start (host tools\n+ client bundle) →"},{"id":"p46s2","text":" uninstall lifecycle against a **throwaway `DSH_HOME`** and\nprints a JSON evidence record. It never "},{"id":"p46s3","text":"touches a real profile."},{"id":"p47s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p48s1","text":"Optional flags: `--source <plugin dir>` (defaults to the cwd) and\n`--pnpm <path>`. It exits non-zero"},{"id":"p48s2","text":" unless all nine checks pass. Results feeding\n`dsh.compatibility.dshReleases` are recorded in\ndocs/C"},{"id":"p48s3","text":" checks pass. Results feeding\n`dsh.compatibility.dshReleases` are recorded in\ndocs/COMPATIBILITY.md."}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
